Once Docker is set up for Render:
GHCR(Github Container Registry)

Create a GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT) with the right package permissions (write packages & delete packages).

### Log in to GitHub Container Registry
docker login ghcr.io --username <GitHub username> --password <Access token>

### Build the image ,can give any name not just portfolio-blog
docker build -t ghcr.io/<GitHub username>/portfolio-blog .

### Push to GitHub Container Registry
docker push ghcr.io/<GitHub username>/portfolio-blog

### Connect to Render
Make sure github docker package is set to public ,click package settings ,change to public

click add webservice on render, existing package, copy package url from ghcr and paste , configure/paste env variables


######  Secure GHCR IMAGE###
Click settings on render ,image then pause, go to github packages ,packages settings,change visibility back to private,go back to render settings image, click Add credentials

name:e.g portfolio-blod-cred
registry:github
username:github username
personal access token:<paste personal access token from github created>